From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lasimeri <217267696+Lasimeri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:40:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] x86/knc: Ethernet over the host/card ring (phi0)

A network device on the ring region's kind-2 channel: frames travel as
u16 length plus payload, padded to 4 bytes, in one byte ring per
direction (docs/spec/ring-protocol.md v1). The driver polls the
host-to-card ring every jiffy from a delayed work item and copies frames
into the card-to-host ring from ndo_start_xmit, dropping when the host
has not drained it. The rings are mapped uncached because the host
writes card memory through the PCIe aperture behind the card's caches
and the core has no CLFLUSH.

The ring layout constants move from the console driver into
asm/knc_ring.h, shared by both, and the console driver's command-line
parser (phi.ring=base,size) is exported so the network device finds
the same region. The host side is phictl's --net bridge to a TAP
device.
